WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.400
- So Al, your new book, I love the title.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.430
Anybody that knows me that sees your book,

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.230
buys your book, reads your
book is going to laugh

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.740
because literally the
thing said most to me

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.690
in my life, in my career is

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.967
the title of your book, "You
Look So Much Better in Person."

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.630
I honestly thought it was just me.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.517
Every time I run into people, they're like

00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:25.910
"You look so much better in person."

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.839
I'm like, "Thank you since
85% of my life is on camera."

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:32.089
(laughter)

00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.090
And they say that to you all the time?

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.538
- Yeah, every day, yeah
I go out and shake hands

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.890
at the Plaza obviously pre-pandemic

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.807
and invariably one person,
at least one person will say,

00:00:43.807 --> 00:00:46.720
"Oh my gosh, you look so
much better in person."

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.553
- Every time.

00:00:47.553 --> 00:00:50.070
- And I know they mean it as a compliment

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:50.903
- Absolutely.

00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:52.353
- so I don't want to embarrass them.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.710
To your point, I make my living on TV.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.030
- That's what I say!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.560
- So, that I look better
here just means that

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.010
I'm scaring small children on television.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.770
- Yeah, like what does that mean?

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.757
And they're always like, "You're
shorter and you're smaller,

00:01:09.757 --> 00:01:10.590
"you're more petite"

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.127
and I'm just like, "Do
I look like an Amazon?"

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.460
Or they say that at concerts.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.347
They'll come backstage
after a concert and be like

00:01:18.347 --> 00:01:20.670
"Oh my god, you sound better in person."

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.510
I'm like "Great because most of it's not

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.277
in person, so solid."

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.693
It's amazing.

